The integrator has three ingredients:

Quasi-static singularity extraction. Subtract the leading 1/k_ρ asymptote analytically (transform of C/k_ρ is C/(2πρ)), integrate the remainder numerically.

Real-axis head. Adaptive quad from 0 to 6·n_max·k₀, with breakpoints at material wavenumbers and pole locations.

Hankel-split tail. J₀ = (H₀⁽¹⁾ + H₀⁽²⁾)/2, each H₀ integrated on a ray into the appropriate half-plane so the oscillatory tail decays exponentially. Deformation angle θ = 0.5 rad.

Poles are located as zeros of the kernel denominator (η↑+η↓ for TM, ζ↑+ζ↓ for TE), which is by construction what the Sommerfeld contour needs.

