## 3.12 Retraction — The LC "Identity" Was a Tautology

`line_rlgc` defines `L = Z0·β/ω` with `Z0 = β/(ωC)`. Therefore `L·C = β²/ω² = n_m²/c²` **identically, for any C whatsoever**. Checking it against `n_m²/c²` re-tests `n_m` and nothing else — it is an algebraic identity of the extraction, not a second measurement.

